From 6f742e2e7d077f7360306d30390b1388bf98d4fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: m5agent <m5agent@m5stack.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:29:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hw/m5stopwatch: add AtomS3R-M12 board with OV3660 camera
 model

AtomS3R-M12 (C126-M12) is the M12-lens variant of the AtomS3R camera
controller: ESP32-S3-PICO-1-N8R8, GC9107 128x128 panel, BMI270 + BMM150,
and an OV3660 sensor on the same DVP/SCCB pin group as AtomS3R-CAM
(vsync G10, href G14, xclk G21, pclk G40, D0..D7, SCCB SDA G12 / SCL G9,
power G18).

The new m5atoms3rm12 machine reuses the AtomS3R-CAM controller, panel,
PSRAM, LCD_CAM and dedicated SCCB bridge, but populates only the M12
hardware inventory (BMM150 0x10, BMI270 0x68, OV3660 0x3c) and binds the
LCD_CAM device to the OV3660 geometry.

The OV3660 I2C slave model implements the 16-bit SCCB register space used
by esp32-camera (SCCB_Read16/Write16): two address bytes, then the data
byte; read transactions keep the pointer written by the preceding write.
PID 0x3660 is served from read-only 0x300A/0x300B, a software reset in
0x3008 bit 7 clears volatile state, and the DVP output width/height in
registers 0x3808-0x380b are decoded and published to LCD_CAM, which
latches them at CAM_START.

Guest evidence: official UIFlow2 v2.5.4 AtomS3R-CAM image (whose M5Burner
entry declares "UIFlow2 for AtomS3R-CAM and AtomS3R-M12") runs on this
machine and its camera module detects OV3660 at 0x3c (PID 0x3660) and
returns QQVGA/VGA/HD frames matching the host-reconstructed DVP waveform,
plus five distinct streamed frames.  The M5Burner "AtomS3R-CAM M12 User
Demo" (usb_webcam, IDF v5.1.4) also boots on this machine, its own
esp32-camera detects/initializes the OV3660, and its internal I2C scan
sees exactly 0x10/0x3c/0x68; its MJPEG/UVC frame path is not modeled
(NO-SOI) and full demo behaviour remains NOT RUN.
